	(text "Power entry: +5V from an external 5 V supply, +24V for the wind sensor (10-30 V),\n+3V3 from the FireBeetle regulator. PWR_FLAGs mark the external sources.\nB1 plugs into the FireBeetle's own battery socket (J3 is that socket, not a separate part)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 251.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b2d5da79-a1dc-456d-8bf8-437fae08a6e6")
	)
	(text "NOTES\n- Valve GPIOs come from CONFIG_DYNAMIC_VALVE_GPIO_LIST = 1,14,18,21,22,16,17,5\n  (valves 1-8, CONFIG_DEVICE_MAX_VALVES = 8). All 8 relay channels are valves.\n- GPIO 16/17 are UART0: the console runs on USB Serial/JTAG.\n- No safe GPIO is left: more valves, the 24 VAC converter enable,\n  mains-detect, battery sense and the LCD need an I2C expander / I2C ADC.\n- Relay contacts are not in the relay module symbol: J2 pin 1 -> COM1..8,\n  NO1..8 -> valves 1..8, J2 pin 2 -> valve common.\n- IO6/IO7 reserved for the ESP32-S3 UART link (not drawn yet).\n- The I2C bus uses header pins 28/29; pins 9/10 are the same signals.\n- I2C pull-ups are on the breakout boards.\n  BMP581: SDO=GND (address 0x46), CS=3V3 (I2C mode).\n- 1.8k/3.3k dividers scale the 0-5 V sensor outputs to 0-3.24 V.\n- Not drawn yet: ESP32-S3, LCD2004, 24 VAC converter, 24 V battery path."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "180e8f41-84f5-4a0f-9a96-13f1530ac176")
	)
